A null value prints as <null>, the description of Foundation's NSNull.

Yams reads `published:` as NSNull. FrontmatterCommand.formatValue falls
through to "\(value)" for anything that is not an array, and the
description of NSNull is the literal text <null>. So the command hands
back a word that is in no YAML document and that no reader of the file
would recognise.

It should print `null`, the word YAML itself uses.
